{"id": "EUVD-2026-104683", "enisaUuid": "69e40ba8-f095-3e17-9135-34ab16195932", "description": "JoySafeter through 1.0.0 contains a remote code execution vulnerability that allows authenticated users to run operating system commands via an unsandboxed execute tool in Copilot standard mode. Attackers can self-register, select standard mode in the WebSocket chat.start extension, and have the agent invoke subprocess.run with shell=True on the host to access other tenants' data and server secrets.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T00:46:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T21:04:54", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://www.lasso.security/vulnerability-database/cve-2026-109443", "https://github.com/jd-opensource/JoySafeter/blob/12234a11a9d96acef85577afb1fa5682169d6171/backend/app/core/agent/backends/utils/command_executor.py#L110", "https://github.com/jd-opensource/JoySafeter/blob/12234a11a9d96acef85577afb1fa5682169d6171/backend/app/services/copilot_service.py#L106", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/joysafeter-through-1.0.0-authenticated-rce-via-copilot-standard-mode-shell"], "aliases": ["GHSA-qmmc-575c-v2h8", "CVE-2026-109443"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.71, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "cca7dfea-eaf1-3d66-beee-42509e2b7bcc", "product": {"name": "JoySafeter", "vendor": {"name": "jd-opensource"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.0.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ec4ba929-1c14-31a9-9031-611035c261a3", "vendor": {"name": "jd-opensource"}}], "isExploited": false}